Pages
=====

One file per route in src/pages/. For each: what staff do there, what it
calls, and what it listens to.


Login  /login
-------------

src/pages/Login.tsx

Staff email and password against the admin login endpoint. On success the
token pair is stored and the router sends the user to /app. Any failure is
shown inline; there is no separate error route.

	calls     useAuth().login -> POST /admin/login
	realtime  none


Overview  /app
--------------

src/pages/Overview.tsx

The landing dashboard. Counts and shortcuts across the three things staff
touch daily: challenges, the quest bank, and the activity catalogue.

	calls     getAllChallenges, getPendingApprovals,
	          getAllQuests, getAllActivities
	realtime  none directly; the sidebar's pending badge is live


Challenges  /app/challenges
---------------------------

src/pages/Challenges.tsx

The challenge library, grouped by season. Cards show the image, window,
participant count and status, and link into the detail view. Delete is behind
a confirmation dialog.

	calls     getAllChallenges, deleteChallenge
	realtime  none

Season grouping uses the same rule as the backend's utils/season.ts. If one
changes the other must.


Create challenge  /app/challenges/new
-------------------------------------

src/pages/CreateChallenge.tsx

The largest form in the console. Captures name, description, type and
category, goal and unit, points per unit, start and end dates, venue and
instructor, whether the result requires staff validation, the XP reward, and
the three podium values. Images are picked from a curated bank rather than
uploaded, with suggestions filtered by challenge type.

	calls     createChallenge
	realtime  none

Creating a challenge causes the backend to notify every student, by socket and
by push. Staff should be told that publishing is a broadcast; the form has a
note to that effect and it should stay there.


Challenge detail  /app/challenge/:id
------------------------------------

src/pages/ChallengeDetail.tsx

One challenge: hero image, facts panel, podium rewards, and the live standings
board with avatars, flags, faculty labels and results.

	calls     getChallengeById, getChallengeLeaderboard,
	          getChallengeParticipants
	realtime  validation:resolved, validation:submitted,
	          challenge:participants

Standings are rendered by AdminLeaderboardBoard in showResult mode so the
submitted figure appears next to each student.


Validations  /app/validations
-----------------------------

src/pages/Validations.tsx

The staff work queue. Every supervised result a student has submitted and no
one has judged. Approve pushes the points to the leaderboard; reject sends it
back. Both are behind a confirmation dialog because neither is reversible from
this screen.

	calls     getPendingApprovals, approveParticipant, rejectParticipant
	realtime  validation:submitted, validation:resolved

This is the page that must never show stale data, which is why it subscribes
to both events rather than only to the one it causes.


Leaderboards  /app/leaderboards
-------------------------------

src/pages/Leaderboards.tsx

Three tabs. Faculty groups students by faculty; Campus is the individual
standing; Challenges shows the board for any single challenge.

	calls     getFacultyLeaderboard, getCampusLeaderboard,
	          getAllChallenges, getChallengeLeaderboard
	realtime  validation:resolved, challenge:created

All three tabs refresh on the same events, because an approval anywhere moves
every board.


Daily quests  /app/quests
-------------------------

src/pages/Quests.tsx

Two halves. The top shows the quests students see today, locked. The bottom
lets staff hand-pick tomorrow's three: swap a slot, remove one, or fill an
empty slot from the bank. Below that is the bank itself, searchable, with add
and delete.

	calls     getDailyQuests, setDailyQuests, clearDailyOverride,
	          getAllQuests, addQuest, removeQuest
	realtime  quests:updated

Today is deliberately read-only. Changing the set a student has already
started their day against would invalidate progress they can see on screen.
Editing tomorrow writes a daily_quest_overrides row; clearing it returns that
date to the deterministic rotation. See the backend's docs/gamification.md.


Not implemented
---------------

The sidebar in src/components/SideBar.tsx lists two more items:

	/app/activities   Activities
	/app/settings     Settings

Neither route exists in App.tsx, so both fall through to the catch-all and
redirect to Overview. The activity catalogue and admin account management were
in scope and are served by existing backend endpoints (/area and /admin
respectively). Building these two pages is the largest single piece of
outstanding work in this repository. See docs/maintenance.md.